{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016XzfDBbjguK39bVCDWTjRx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So the result is still empty — meaning `capturedResult` is NOT being updated on re-render. The `get result()` getter is returning the old object. This means the re-render either isn't happening or `capturedResult` isn't being updated.\n\nThe issue could be that React is NOT re-rendering the component because `config` is a prop, and React might see it as the same object in some way... No, we're passing `{ config: newConfig }` which is a new object.\n\nWait — I think the real issue is that the getter on the returned object is working fine, but `capturedResult` is a copy. Let me check if maybe the issue is with strict mode double-rendering or something.\n\nActually — I bet I know. The `result` getter is in the returned object from `mountUpload`, which is destructured as `{ result, rerender }`. When you destructure `result` from `{ get result() { ... } }`, you get the VALUE at that point, not the getter! The getter is only active when accessed via the object property.\n\nWait, no — destructuring `{ result, rerender }` would evaluate `result` eagerly if it were a getter. But looking at the code:\n\n```js\nconst { result, rerender } = mountUpload(initialConfig)\n```\n\nThis calls `get result()` once and assigns the value. After that, `result` is just a plain variable.\n\nBut other tests like `useLiveFormReact.test.ts` use the same pattern successfully. Let me check how..."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":78493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":422},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aef57bc1-a1d6-4ff6-aae1-abea1eae50ab","uuid":"f7a6ade7-a7ed-434e-ad9b-539ef8414623"}
