{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VkV6BkwtJdyjjcDq2wXpEL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I see! In the form test, it returns `get form()` and the tests use `form` (not destructured as `const { form } = ...`). Let me check:\n\nLooking at test line 198: `const { form } = mountForm(formData)` - this DOES destructure. But in that case, `form` is also evaluated eagerly. Yet the form tests pass because `useLiveForm` returns an object with GETTERS (like `get isValid()`) that close over the mutable `storeRef`. So even though `form` is a snapshot, its getters read the latest mutable state.\n\nMy `useLiveUpload` hook returns plain values like `entries: uploadConfig.entries || []`. This is a snapshot — not a getter. So when the test destructures `result`, it gets the snapshot from the initial render.\n\nThe fix is: either make the test access `result` through the getter on each assertion (don't destructure), or make the hook return an object with getters. The simpler fix is to not destructure in the test:\n\nActually wait — looking more carefully at the test:\n```js\nconst { result, rerender } = mountUpload(initialConfig)\n```\n\n`result` is destructured from an object with `get result()`. In JS, destructuring DOES call the getter. So `result` is a plain value — the return value of `useLiveUpload` from the first render. After `rerender`, `capturedResult` changes, but `result` still points to the old object.\n\nBut `mountForm` has the same pattern! `const { form } = mountForm(formData)`. After `rerender(newForm)`, tests like:\n```js\nexpect(form.field(\"name\").value).toBe(\"Jane Smith\")\n```\nwork because `form` is a snapshot of the `UseLiveFormReactReturn` object, but that object's `field()` method reads from the mutable `storeRef`. So even though `form` doesn't change, the mutable state it references does change.\n\nFor my upload hook, I need the return object to read from the latest config through a ref. Let me update the hook to use a similar pattern."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":78915,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1064},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aef57bc1-a1d6-4ff6-aae1-abea1eae50ab","uuid":"dd4501b0-ffd6-4ea2-9cc3-3ecd21fa32c7"}
